# the bridge (cf_bridge.c, cf_synth.c): ucas's engines behind the C
# frontend (README "C frontend", "Engines"), each candidate with its
# engine's certificate; all engines run by default.  The synthesis (CEGIS
# over the intrinsics) is budgeted in sketches, so what it finds does not
# depend on the machine; cfront's own proof budget is CPU time, and the
# synthesis grows the node table, so each target runs in a file (a
# process) of its own: cfbridge_icl.ucas, cfbridge_zen4.ucas.
c optimize cfront/bridge.c nofile budget 120
# opt-in: the float sum in closed form, applied (an approximation)
c optimize cfront/bridge.c nofile approx engines loops budget 120
# one engine at a time; none
c optimize nofile engines ring
```c
int crt(unsigned x) { return x % 4 == 1 && x % 9 == 4; }
int never(unsigned x) { return (x * 6u) == 9u; }
```
c optimize nofile engines none
```c
int crt(unsigned x) { return x % 4 == 1 && x % 9 == 4; }
```
c optimize nofile engines bogus
```c
int f(int x) { return x; }
```
